WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.260
Popkin has a console for the people who run it. This is how they get in.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.561
Lena opens the audit log, and the console asks who she is: her staff email first.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.305
A code goes to that address, and it works for ten minutes.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.737
Then the page she asked for opens. The audit log lists every action taken in the

00:00:32.737 --> 00:00:35.346
console, newest first, with who did it.

00:00:35.546 --> 00:00:38.544
It is kept for two years, and nobody can edit it.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.684
Admins and roles lists everyone who can sign in, with their role and when they were

00:00:46.684 --> 00:00:47.661
last active.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.609
An Owner adds an admin with their popkin dot app address. They are invited until

00:00:56.609 --> 00:00:58.695
they first sign in with a code.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.958
Changing a role says what changes, and asks for a reason, which goes into the audit

00:01:08.958 --> 00:01:09.497
log.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.092
What each role can do sets Owner, Support and Viewer side by side.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.918
On a phone it is one column. On a desktop, a sidebar names the pages.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.682
What the tests prove: a right code that is not an admin's is turned away, and the

00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:40.774
console always keeps one Owner.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.017
That is journey twenty-four. Popkin is a free platform for pop-up communities.
